<section class="w-full max-w-page mx-auto px-6 mt-content" aria-label="Key facts">
    <dl class="cs-facts">
        <div class="cs-facts__item"><dt>What</dt><dd>Internal AI assistant for Dell sellers</dd></div>
        <div class="cs-facts__item"><dt>Users</dt><dd>About 20,000 sellers</dd></div>
        <div class="cs-facts__item"><dt>Built by</dt><dd>Dell, in-house</dd></div>
        <div class="cs-facts__item"><dt>Live since</dt><dd>Sept 2025 at the latest</dd></div>
    </dl>
</section>

<section class="w-full max-w-page mx-auto px-6 mt-section" aria-labelledby="br-labels">
    <h2 id="br-labels" class="cs-heading">How to read this</h2>
    <ul class="br-legend">
        <li><span class="br-tag br-tag--confirmed">Confirmed</span>Dell said it on the record, or a credible outlet reported it, and we read the source ourselves.</li>
        <li><span class="br-tag br-tag--unverified">Unverified</span>We've only seen it second-hand. Check it before repeating it.</li>
        <li><span class="br-tag br-tag--view">Our view</span>Our own inference. Treat it as opinion.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="w-full max-w-page mx-auto px-6 mt-section" aria-labelledby="br-short">
    <h2 id="br-short" class="cs-heading">The short version</h2>
    <ol class="br-points">
        <li class="br-point"><div>
            <h3 class="br-point__title">Sales Chat is real, and it's now how Dell sellers find information.</h3>
            <p class="br-point__body">It's Dell's own internal AI assistant, rolled out to all of its roughly 20,000 sellers. Dell switched off the older seller tools when it launched.<span class="br-tag br-tag--confirmed">Confirmed</span></p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="br-point"><div>
            <h3 class="br-point__title">It reuses content Dell already has. It doesn't create anything new.</h3>
            <p class="br-point__body">Dell describes it as pulling content together from across its systems. Sellers use it to find information, summarise it, draft content and automate emails.<span class="br-tag br-tag--confirmed">Confirmed</span></p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="br-point"><div>
            <h3 class="br-point__title">Nothing in public says it has replaced agency work.</h3>
            <p class="br-point__body">That we've seen work drop off is our observation, not something we can prove from outside.<span class="br-tag br-tag--view">Our view</span></p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="br-point"><div>
            <h3 class="br-point__title">The next wave is aimed at partners.</h3>
            <p class="br-point__body">Dell's new partner platform, launching in the second half of 2026, is run by "a family of AI assistants".<span class="br-tag br-tag--confirmed">Confirmed</span> That puts channel marketing in the frame next.<span class="br-tag br-tag--view">Our view</span></p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="br-point"><div>
            <h3 class="br-point__title">Lean into what a chat tool can't do, and widen the client base.</h3>
            <p class="br-point__body">In the short to medium term, pitch and run more cutting-edge AI events for Dell and NVIDIA, such as hackathons and hands-on labs, plus complex, expert-led content like e-guides. In the longer term, win clients beyond Dell.<span class="br-tag br-tag--view">Our view</span></p>
        </div></li>
    </ol>
</section>

